{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The chiefs of Edom, the mighty men of Moab.</b> Now did they have anything to fear at all, since Israel was not coming against them? Rather, because of the distress — they were aggrieved and pained over the glory of Israel (Yalkut Shimoni)." "<b>Melted away.</b> Dissolved, as in ״בְּרָבִיבִים תְּמוֹגְגֶנָּה״ (Psalms 65). They said: Against us they are coming, to destroy us and inherit our land (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:27.817615555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}